cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SuRT-GeoHarmonizer, cite the software release identified below.
title: >-
  SuRT-GeoHarmonizer: auditable administrative-scale Earth-data harmonization
  and provenance labelling
version: 1.3.0
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tuyishime
    given-names: Audre Prince
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-0799-3140"
abstract: >-
  SuRT-GeoHarmonizer is an open R and Python command-line workflow for
  converting heterogeneous environmental rasters into consistent,
  provenance-labelled administrative-unit GeoJSON layers. It provides a
  provider-agnostic raster and polygon interface, Rwanda reference builders
  for CHIRPS rainfall, ERA5-Land temperature, MODIS NDVI, and HAND terrain,
  fail-closed evidence classification, positive and negative tests,
  independent release-contract validation, and versioned integrity records.
  The software produces descriptive environmental summaries and does not
  claim validated hazards, forecasts, epidemiological effects, or operational
  recommendations.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/PrinceAudre/surt-virtual-rwanda-repro"
url: "https://github.com/PrinceAudre/surt-virtual-rwanda-repro"
keywords:
  - geospatial software
  - environmental data harmonization
  - data provenance
  - zonal statistics
  - reproducible research
  - GeoJSON
